      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-222135",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$, $B$, and $C$ be sets. Prove that\n$(A\u2229C)\u222a(B\u2229C)\u2286(A\u222aB)\u2229C$.\n\nGiven any $x \u2208 (A\u2229C)\u222a(B\u2229C)$, we have the following sequence of implications:\n\n$(x \u2208 A\u222aC)\u2227(x \u2208 B\u222aC)$ {{field-1}}"
